WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.220
Start with SEAL open. This workspace is
empty.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:10.480
Select Load demo workspace to add the
sample sequences, notebook pages,

3
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.840
and saved alignments. The examples use
synthetic data.

4
00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:21.140
In the left sidebar, expand SEAL Sample Lab
and open Synthetic Reporter.

5
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.800
The center of the window shows an Entry.

6
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.740
An Entry groups related sequence blocks and
notes.

7
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:33.210
Select Synthetic Reporter DNA. The
Inspector on the right shows information

8
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.660
for that block. In Overview, check the
sequence length, molecule type,

9
00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:44.500
and base composition. The example DNA has
seven hundred and twenty bases.

10
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:48.120
The sidebar also opens other parts of your
workspace.

11
00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:53.420
Notebook contains lab notes. Alignments
contains saved sequence comparisons,

12
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.540
including examples with Sanger reads.

13
00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.040
Return to Synthetic Reporter to continue
working with its sequences.

14
00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.535
You can move between these pages while
keeping the same workspace open.
